      "refersTo": "query-field",
      "description": "The phone request field and its enclosing composer outline; the complete form adds ruled condition rows.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-composer\"><textarea class=\"ds-query\" aria-label=\"What would you like to do?\" placeholder=\"A quiet walk by the river\"></textarea></div>",
      "css": ".ds-composer{border:1px solid var(--line-strong,#9eacbf);border-radius:14px;background:#fff;}.ds-composer:focus-within{border-color:var(--accent,#245fc5);}.ds-query{box-sizing:border-box;display:block;width:100%;min-height:100px;max-height:168px;border:0;border-radius:14px 14px 0 0;padding:17px 16px;background:#fff;color:var(--ink,#202631);font:400 17px/1.4 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,\"Noto Sans\",\"Helvetica Neue\",Arial,sans-serif;resize:vertical;caret-color:var(--accent,#245fc5);}.ds-query::placeholder{color:#5a6575;opacity:1;}.ds-query:hover{background:#fff;}.ds-query:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent,#245fc5);outline-offset:-4px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Language navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "language-navigation",
      "description": "Shared RU/KK/EN controls with a neutral selected fill and 44px targets.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-languages\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Interface language\"><button aria-pressed=\"true\">RU</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">KK</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">EN</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-languages{display:flex;gap:0;background:#fff;}.ds-languages button{min-width:44px;min-height:44px;padding:8px;border:0;border-radius:7px;background:transparent;color:var(--ink-2,#495362);font:600 12px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,\"Noto Sans\",\"Helvetica Neue\",Arial,sans-serif;cursor:pointer;}.ds-languages button[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{background:#f0f2f5;color:var(--ink,#202631);}.ds-languages button:hover{cursor:pointer;}.ds-languages button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent,#245fc5);outline-offset:3px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Filter chip",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "filter-chip",
      "description": "Rectangular filter with a pale cobalt selected state.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-chip\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Step free</button>",
      "css": ".ds-chip{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;min-height:44px;padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #c5cedb;border-radius:7px;background:#fff;color:var(--ink,#202631);font:400 13px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,\"Noto Sans\",\"Helvetica Neue\",Arial,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color 150ms ease-out,border-color 150ms ease-out,transform 100ms ease-out;}.ds-chip[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{color:var(--accent-strong,#194b9f);background:var(--accent-soft,#edf3ff);border-color:var(--accent,#245fc5);}.ds-chip:hover{background:var(--accent-soft,#edf3ff);border-color:var(--accent,#245fc5);}.ds-chip:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent,#245fc5);outline-offset:3px;}.ds-chip:active{transform:scale(.97);}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-chip{transition:none;transform:none!important;}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Itinerary stop",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "itinerary-stop",
      "description": "Flat numbered stop row; yellow applies only to the first actual routed stop. Text here is a neutral preview label.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-stop\" tabindex=\"-1\"><span class=\"ds-rank\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1</span><h3 class=\"ds-stop-title\">Place name</h3><p class=\"ds-reason\">The server explains why this stop fits.</p></article>",
      "css": ".ds-stop{position:relative;border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line,#dfe4eb);border-radius:0;padding:22px 0 22px 52px;background:transparent;color:var(--ink,#202631);font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,\"Noto Sans\",\"Helvetica Neue\",Arial,sans-serif;box-shadow:none;}.ds-rank{position:absolute;left:0;top:22px;display:grid;place-items:center;width:35px;height:35px;border:1px solid var(--gold,#f2b705);border-radius:50%;background:var(--gold,#f2b705);font-size:17px;font-weight:700;}.ds-stop-title{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:23px;line-height:1.22;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.025em;overflow-wrap:anywhere;}.ds-reason{margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;font-weight:400;}.ds-stop:hover{box-shadow:none;}.ds-stop:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent,#245fc5);outline-offset:3px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Confirmed opening badge",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "badge-open",
      "description": "Green opening badge for open_status open with high confidence only.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-open\">Open</span>",
      "css": ".ds-open{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;border-radius:5px;padding:3px 5px;background:var(--open-bg,#e2f3e8);color:var(--open-ink,#13633a);font:700 12px/1.4 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,\"Noto Sans\",\"Helvetica Neue\",Arial,sans-serif;}.ds-open::before{content:\"\";width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:currentColor;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Map stop",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "map-stop",
      "description": "Circular map stop; selecting it uses the active cobalt state.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-map-stop\" aria-label=\"Stop 2\">2</button>",
      "css": ".ds-map-stop{box-sizing:border-box;display:grid;place-items:center;width:34px;height:34px;padding:0;border:2px solid var(--accent,#245fc5);border-radius:50%;background:#fff;color:var(--accent-strong,#194b9f);box-shadow:0 3px 8px #20263126;font:700 16px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,\"Noto Sans\",\"Helvetica Neue\",Arial,sans-serif;cursor:pointer;}.ds-map-stop:hover{cursor:pointer;}.ds-map-stop:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent,#245fc5);outline-offset:3px;}.ds-map-stop:active{background:var(--accent,#245fc5);color:#fff;transform:scale(1.15);}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A city guide, step by step",
    "overview": "Qadam uses a white daylight surface, confident system typography, cobalt wayfinding and a yellow start action. Fine rules and an openly spaced numbered sequence keep a short walk easy to scan. The team mark is two cobalt steps with a gold dot beside the QADAM wordmark.\n\nThis captures the integrated application in `web/index.html`, with `styles.css` followed by the scoped `city-guide.css`. The approved prototype supplies the direction; the current production source supplies these tokens and components. Other prototype screens and its retired hexagon mark are outside this system capture.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White reading surfaces and graphite text.",
      "Cobalt wayfinding, yellow start, explicit factual status.",
      "Ruled controls, continuous routed stops and a quiet map.",
      "System fonts and SVG details with accessible touch controls."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Color Meaning Rule",
        "body": "Yellow marks the start action and first routed stop. Green means high-confidence open; purple identifies AI provenance.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The System Type Rule",
        "body": "Use the existing system stack and preserve Kazakh character coverage.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Reading Rule",
        "body": "Keep route content flat; use elevation where controls float over the map.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use the current steps-and-dot mark and QADAM wordmark.",
      "**Do** preserve the cobalt, yellow and factual-status color meanings.",
      "**Do** keep route content flat, numbered and visibly connected only when routed.",
      "**Do** preserve visible focus, 44px touch actions and static reduced-motion states.",
      "**Do** use real server facts and retain uncertain opening information."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** apply the prototype's retired logo or semantic color values to this integration.",
      "**Don't** give alternatives the route rail or first-stop yellow treatment.",
      "**Don't** represent direct estimates with the graph path's solid stroke.",
      "**Don't** use decorative footsteps as live location or progress data.",
      "**Don't** introduce invented photos, reviews or ratings."
    ]
  }
}
